art protocol was complete: healthy pre-state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a changed post-restart identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered services/readiness were all captured.","evidence_ids":["cmd-95dbac938d7a423f","cmd-9638a1bd62a84fe4","cmd-b68a89f9aa814d12","cmd-4c576cb9d8564d99","cmd-7353fa4c4e4c4f03","cmd-7a301387a55b4844","cmd-e35868a51bf6495e","cmd-140439c20ab24d3a","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct transition and final-state evidence. The supplied programs are healthy, enabled systemd services, and repeated observations—including a cold start and reboot—show the database reaching readiness before the API starts. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 was complete and internally consistent.","limitations":["The supplied programs expose no separate business-data or cluster query interface; restart recovery was therefore validated through service state, expected managed processes, readiness state, and startup journals. This is adequate for the supplied single-node marker-based programs."]}
